Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Current Build Host Pilot P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 1b4987f2-860a-4650-a24f-c188a565c49b
@ [canonical_uuid] 4cf12917-73e8-4505-9228-f94d981143bd

& [Why]
  + the user needs visible evidence that current Cantor work can run on the intended host and eventually direct its own build process
  + a preserved older Needle2 deployment proves an integration ancestor but cannot prove current artifact portability or self-work readiness

& [WhyThisSlice]
  + the independent A8 verifier is current substantial provider-free work with strict retained evidence and no external effects, making it the safest first cross-host executable
  + an isolated versioned root allows direct comparison while preserving historical evidence and a clean later escalation path

& [WhyNotMore]
  + remote source compilation would first require toolchain installation and large caches; autonomous build mutation would conflate portability with still-unproved work authority
  + persistent service or model changes add operational and security variables that do not answer the first question

& [Decision]
  + authorize implementation after formation publication and authorize live installation only after local implementation gates and publication; keep self-work and provider mutation locked
